//! The `scroll-padding-block-end` property defines offsets for the end edge in the block dimension
//! of the _optimal viewing region_ of the scrollport: the region used as the target region for
//! placing things in view of the user. This allows the author to exclude regions of the scrollport
//! that are obscured by other content (such as fixed-positioned toolbars or sidebars) or to put more
//! breathing room between a targeted element and the edges of the scrollport.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: relative to the scroll container's scrollport.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The offset is determined by the user agent. This will generally be 0px, but a user agent
//! is able to detect and do something else if a non-zero value is more appropriate.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <length-percentage [0,∞]>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1/#propdef-scroll-padding-block-end
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/scroll-padding-block-end
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

